# WEBSITE READINESS

Goal: make the RSARBOS manual underwriting website ready for staging/live verification.

## Readiness Result
- Status: ready for staging verification.
- Build check: passing with `npm run build` in `rsarbos-mission-control`.
- Primary workflow: visitor submits a manual underwriting request, receives confirmation, and the request routes to operations.
- Intake route: `uw.requests@rsarbos.com`
- Support route: `support@rsarbos.com`
- Payment confirmation route: manual settlement / payment-status ledger confirmation.

## Fulfilled Scope
- Public domain now serves the RSARBOS manual underwriting website instead of the internal founder dashboard.
- Mission Control is routed to `/mission-control` behind a password gate.
- Website mission-control tab now carries explicit readiness metrics for intake routing, support routing, payment confirmation copy, and funnel tracking.
- Website founder tasks now reflect the live verification work instead of a vague copy audit.
- Website operations files now identify the staging/live verification state and the next action.
- UI now shows a website readiness checklist when the Website tab is selected.
- Production build was verified.

## Public / Private Boundary
- `/` is public and must sell the manual underwriting service.
- `/mission-control` is private and must remain an internal founder operations tool.
- Set `VITE_MISSION_CONTROL_PASSWORD` in Vercel to control the Mission Control gate password.

## Remaining Live Checks
